The bundled libsqlite3-sys bindings retain their upstream MIT license in
vendor/libsqlite3-sys/LICENSE. The SQLite amalgamation carries the upstream
public-domain dedication in its source. The bundled amalgamation is SQLite
3.54.1, as identified in sqlite3.c and sqlite3.h.

See vendor/libsqlite3-sys/README.md for the upstream blob and SHA3-256
digest of the amalgamation, and https://sqlite.org/copyright.html for
the SQLite copyright statement.

Cargo fetches the remaining packages from crates.io as pinned in Cargo.lock.
Their declared licenses and packaged notices are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.

The original SOQ.MARKET wallet source is provided under the workspace MIT
license. The browser boundary module extracts the corresponding application
integration code. The Node WASM conformance tests derive from the application
tests and use synthetic funding data.

The fips204 source (IntegrityChain / Eric Schorn) is pinned to
241af0d25efe54a3c99c6a7a8bd2fba3295f6951. Its manifest was adjusted upstream
in SOQ.MARKET to remove workspace, development dependencies, benches and
profiles. The RustCrypto sha3 source is pinned to
1637e892b5658941d04a4d895165b66780c7d7ab and keccak to
40c50c16410392439e2ac4ee0286285db479a106. All three retain their upstream
MIT and Apache-2.0 license files alongside the code.

The BIP 39 English word list in crates/soq-wallet/src/bip39-english.txt is from
https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039/english.txt. BIP 39
identifies its license as MIT and credits Marek Palatinus, Pavol Rusnak,
Aaron Voisine, and Sean Bowe.

The public ML-DSA-44 fixture in tests/fixtures/official-mldsa44.txt was
generated using Soqucoin Core cryptographic code from revision
ecd502e43a88396cafb50cf4879d22d9b028dafe. It contains a public key and a
signature for synthetic inputs. Soqucoin Core source is external.
